<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n112810" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωλ-άς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">άδος</span>, ἡ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>lurking in a hole,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀραχναίη, σίλφη,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				9.233
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Eryc.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				251
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Even.
			</span></i>), etc.: of the bear, <i>lying torpid in its cave,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Theoc.
				1.115
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hymn.Is.</u>
				46
			</span></i>; metaph., of a <i>shy</i> maiden (opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόρνη</span>)
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">, φωλάδα παρθενικήν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>AP</u>
					11.34
				</span></i>
			 (<i><span class="en">
				Phld.
			</span></i>); <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀγκύρας φωλάδας,</span> of
			anchors <i>buried in the sand,</i> ib.<i><span class="en">
				10.2
			</span></i> (<i><span class="en">
				Antip.Sid.
			</span></i>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> as
				Subst., a mollusc <i>that makes holes in stones,
				Lithodomus,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				3.88a
			</span></i>: <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> has <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωλαΐδες,</span> from a
			confusion of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωλάδες</span> and <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωλίδες.</span>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>full of holes</i> or <i>lurking places,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέτρη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Nonn.
					<u>D.</u>
					1.163
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕλη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					6.270
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				22.116
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔκθορε φωλάδος κοίτης,</span>
			of a lion, <i><span class="en">
				Babr.
				82.3
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωλάς: εἶδος νόσου</span> (i.e. 
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωλεία</span>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				1
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
